      "writtenOn": "2015-07-14T15:45:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seems like we should at least clip the copy/transmit to the size of our output buffer.  Many DMA implementations will just retransmit the last byte of the buffer over and over.  Which will result in a garbage response, but that\u0027s going to happen anyway.  At least clipping stops us leaking other potentially important TPM state via a read buffer overrun.",
